.TH BOOTLOG 1 "2026-10-31" "bootlog 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bootlog \- narrate today's git activity as an operating system boot log
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootlog
[\fB\-\-since\fR \fIEXPR\fR] [\fB\-\-speed\fR \fIMS\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans the configured roots for git repositories, reads what happened in them
today, and prints it in the shape of a kernel boot log: mounted volumes for
repositories with commits, warnings for uncommitted files, and a final target
line with the totals.
.PP
The framing is fiction; the facts are not. Every line comes from
.BR git (1)
run against a repository that exists on disk. A day with no commits says so
rather than inventing activity.
.PP
Timings in the left column are generated from the date, so the same day always
renders the same log. They are not measurements of anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-since " EXPR"
How far back to look. Any git date expression, e.g.
.IR midnight ", " "\(dq2 days ago\(dq" ", " yesterday .
Default
.IR midnight ,
which is today.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " MS"
Milliseconds between lines when printing to a terminal. Default 25. Use 0 for
instant. Output that is piped or redirected is always instant.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON object on stdout and nothing else.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Plain text. Colour is also suppressed when stdout is not a terminal or when
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help. Works in any argument position.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bootlog/config.json
Written with defaults on first run.
.I roots
is the list of directories to scan (default ~/Developer, ~/cc, ~/code, ~/src,
~/.dotfiles; \(dq~\(dq is expanded, and a root that does not exist is skipped),
.I depth
how many levels below each root to descend before giving up (default 3),
.I author
an optional git author filter (default empty, meaning every author), and
.I os
the name printed on the first line (default
.IR breakOS ).
.SH JSON OUTPUT
One object:
.PP
.RS
{ "generated", "since", "os", "host", "user",
.br
"repos": [ ... ], "totals": { ... } }
.RE
.PP
Each repo is
.IR name ", " path ", " branch ", " dirty " (uncommitted file count), "
.IR commits ", " insertions ", " deletions .
Each commit is
.IR hash ", " subject ", " insertions ", " deletions ;
a merge commit reports 0 and 0 rather than repeating the previous commit's
numbers. Totals are
.IR repos ", " active ", " commits ", " insertions ", " deletions .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, including a day with no commits. 1 when git is missing, when no
configured root exists, on an unknown flag, or when
.B \-\-speed
is negative or not a number.
.SH INSTALLATION
Requires Node 22 or later and
.BR git (1)
on PATH.
.PP
.RS
npx @nitrimandylis/bootlog
.br
npm i \-g @nitrimandylis/bootlog
.br
bun add \-g @nitrimandylis/bootlog
.RE
.PP
A global npm install puts this page in the manpath. From a clone,
.B bun run compile
builds a binary to ~/.bun/bin/bootlog and installs this page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-log (1)
